  "proof_construction": "The explicit diagonal K=diag(i*sgn) is transported through the proved same-lattice real equivalence. K^2=-1 and K^*GK=G are direct identities. K^*G=-i*I gives EF_R(Jx,x)=sum_tau 2*Im(tau(xi))*sum_i normSq(theta(x)(tau)(i)), strictly positive for nonzero x by theta injectivity and proved xi_im_pos. The original coefficient action intertwines with scalar diagonal blocks; real traces are twice real parts of complex traces, and exact negTail cardinality yields the source multiplicities. Native canonical conjugation discharges the helper embedding identity and a single actually constructed B serves all k,m,j.",
  "source_adaptations": [
    "Specialized the source generic Hermitian signature conjugation to the actual diagonal standard frame, with no assumed change-of-basis matrix.",
    "Reused native trace_eq_sum_complexEmbeddings for the half-CM trace formula.",
    "Removed unused Fintype of the outer index from purely pointwise block lemmas and retained it exactly on finite trace statements.",
    "Fixed source sign epsilon=+1 using the existing proved native xi_im_pos, preserving the conjugate-first form and EF(Jx,x)>0 orientation.",
    "Kept all original DomFor action-identification and exact trace-expression premises; they identify the arbitrary A and t and do not assume positivity or a geometric estimate.",
    "The pinned Mathlib TensorProduct.inductionOn replaces the deprecated induction_on alias; its two tmul/add branches subsume the redundant zero case. The exact same warning was observed in the preceding real-coordinate supplier on hosted head 3ad6422. No induction hypothesis or theorem conclusion changes."
  ],
